The elements $x_{j_{n}}\cdots x_{j_{1}}$ can be normalized which produces
the involutions 
\begin{equation}
\widetilde{x_{j_{n}}\cdots x_{j_{1}}}=2^{n}x_{j_{n}}\cdots x_{j_{1}},
\end{equation}%
leading to self adjoint involutions 
\begin{equation}
\left( -1\right) ^{n-1}\widetilde{x_{j_{n}}\cdots x_{j_{1}}}.
\end{equation}

Positive elements that belong to $\mathcal{F}_{\left( 4\right) }$ formed
from elements of $\mathcal{F}_{\left( 2\right) }$ have the following form:
letting 
\begin{equation}
\eta =\left\langle \left\langle \xi \right\rangle \right\rangle _{0}\in 
\mathbb{C}
\end{equation}%
one observes 
\begin{align}
\kappa & =\xi ^{\dagger }\xi =\left\vert \eta \right\vert ^{2}I_{\mathcal{A}%
}+\sum_{\substack{ 1\leq p,q\leq 2r  \\ 0\leq p+q\leq 4}}\sum_{\substack{ %
1\leq j_{1}<\cdots <j_{p}\leq 2r  \\ 1\leq k_{1}<\cdots <k_{q}\leq 2r}}%
\overline{\xi }_{j_{1}\cdots j_{p}}\xi _{k_{1}\cdots k_{q}}x_{j_{p}}\cdots
x_{j_{1}}x_{k_{1}}\cdots x_{k_{q}} \\
& =\left\vert \eta \right\vert ^{2}I_{\mathcal{A}}+\sum_{1\leq j_{1}\leq
2r}\left( \bar{\eta}\overline{\xi }_{j_{1}}+\eta \xi _{j_{1}}\right)
x_{j_{1}}+\sum_{1\leq j_{1}<j_{2}\leq 2r}\left( \eta \xi _{j_{1}j_{2}}-\bar{%
\eta}\overline{\xi }_{j_{1}j_{2}}\right) x_{j_{1}}x_{j_{2}} \\
& +\sum_{1\leq j_{1}<j_{2}<j_{3}\leq 2r}\left( \eta \xi _{j_{1}j_{2}j_{3}}-%
